# Benchmark output files
*.html
context-*.html

# WiCE inputs and the corpus converted from them (see docs/wice-benchmark.md).
# Neither is committed: the cache is ~38 MB of upstream JSONL, and
# dataset_wice.json is a 7 MB *deterministic* product of it — `npm run
# wice:convert` rebuilds it byte-identically, and its metadata carries a sha256
# so a rebuild is verifiable. This is the opposite call from dataset.json, which
# IS committed because live Wikipedia + source fetches make it unreproducible.
# Benchmark *outputs* (results_wice.json, analysis_wice*.json) are not ignored —
# those are findings worth keeping.
benchmark/.wice-cache/
benchmark/dataset_wice.json
